      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.2,
          "en": "Now that we've got our user sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.2,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "and we're protecting routes and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 9.39,
          "en": "it's also time to get back to our expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.39,
          "end": 11.25,
          "en": "because you might remember that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.25,
          "end": 16.25,
          "en": "we tweaked our models to link expenses to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.86,
          "end": 19.65,
          "en": "And right now, that logic is missing in our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.65,
          "end": 21.723,
          "en": "and it's, of course, time to change that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.56,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "For that, let's go back to expenses.server.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "where we have this create expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "or this addExpense function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "where we create a new expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 37.863,
          "en": "Here we now wanna link an expenses to a user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 42.57,
          "en": "For that, I actually expect to get a userID here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 44.91,
          "en": "as an additional argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.91,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "And then in the data we store in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 51.633,
          "en": "we can and should also add the user field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 54.63,
          "en": "And set this equal to an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.63,
          "end": 57.99,
          "en": "where we set connect, our reserved name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.99,
          "end": 59.85,
          "en": "in the Prisma world here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.85,
          "end": 64.097,
          "en": "to another object where we set id equal to userId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 66.9,
          "en": "This might look a bit cryptic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.9,
          "end": 68.94,
          "en": "but in the end, that tells Prisma",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.94,
          "end": 71.58,
          "en": "that this expense, which we're creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.58,
          "end": 75.39,
          "en": "should be connected to an existing user with that ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.39,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "So where the ID of the existing user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "is equal to the userId we're passing in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 81.18,
          "en": "as our argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.18,
          "end": 82.63,
          "en": "That's what we're doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "Now, we don't need to do that when we update expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 88.44,
          "en": "because there the user doesn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 91.14,
          "en": "It's just the details data that changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 93.09,
          "en": "so nothing must be done there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "But it is absolutely something we should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.593,
          "en": "when we add an expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.61,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "When we get expenses, we, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "also wanna make sure that we only get expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 105.69,
          "en": "for the user who's logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.69,
          "end": 108.593,
          "en": "So here we should also get a userId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "and then when we find many expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "I also wanna add a where filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.56,
          "en": "where we check for the userId field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 118.56,
          "end": 121.38,
          "en": "which is also added by Prisma",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 123.63,
          "en": "to our expense object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.63,
          "end": 127.86,
          "en": "that this is equal to the userId we get as an argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.86,
          "end": 130.203,
          "en": "And here we can again use that shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 133.593,
          "en": "So that's another check we should add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "We don't really need to tweak getExpense here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "because at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 140.1,
          "en": "we're not really using that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 142.11,
          "en": "Instead, if we're loading a single expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 142.11,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "we're getting that from the list of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 149.28,
          "en": "due to the logic we added in this $id.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.28,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "or in the ExpenseForm to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 154.35,
          "en": "There we use useMatches to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 158.07,
          "en": "to the existing expenses to find a specific expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.07,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "And since that list of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "will automatically soon only look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 165.66,
          "en": "for expenses for that user thanks to our change here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 165.66,
          "end": 168.414,
          "en": "we won't be able to retrieve any other expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 168.414,
          "end": 170.52,
          "en": "than from that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 170.52,
          "end": 173.253,
          "en": "So no tweaks are needed for getExpense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 176.46,
          "en": "Therefore, with those changes made,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 180.36,
          "en": "we can go back to expenses.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 184.603,
          "en": "and there, we now need to pass the userId to getExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.877,
          "end": 190.877,
          "en": "And to do that, we can tweak requireUserSession a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.06,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "and go to auth.server.js again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 196.62,
          "en": "because there we already got the userId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.62,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "and after checking it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 201.03,
          "en": "we can also return it here so that in the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 203.85,
          "en": "where we are already calling this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 206.76,
          "en": "we don't have to unnecessarily call getUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.76,
          "end": 208.29,
          "en": "from session again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.29,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "Instead, in expenses.jsx, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 213.24,
          "en": "we now get the userId as a result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.24,
          "end": 216.153,
          "en": "from requireUserSession if it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.11,
          "end": 220.653,
          "en": "And we can then pass this userId to getExpenses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 222.06,
          "end": 226.29,
          "en": "We also, of course, need that ID when we add a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.29,
          "end": 229.56,
          "en": "So here in the add route where I call addExpense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.56,
          "end": 232.62,
          "en": "we also must pass in the userId",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.62,
          "end": 236.23,
          "en": "and we can simply again call requireUserSession here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 240.96,
          "en": "and await this to get our userId here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 240.96,
          "end": 244.56,
          "en": "and redirect the user if they would send a request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.56,
          "end": 246.6,
          "en": "without being authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 246.6,
          "end": 249.63,
          "en": "which shouldn't really be possible in this app though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "but nonetheless, we can add this check and get the userId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 255.993,
          "en": "And then use that userId down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.73,
          "end": 260.91,
          "en": "With that, we're linking expenses to users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 264.81,
          "en": "and we're then retrieving expenses for different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.81,
          "end": 266.86,
          "en": "And we can therefore now give this a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 271.803,
          "en": "Save everything and log in as a first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 274.65,
          "en": "And then add a new expense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.65,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "Test, 15.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 279.81,
          "en": "Something like this, and I get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.81,
          "end": 282.87,
          "en": "Cannot read properties of undefined reading headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 285.444,
          "en": "Yep, the problem is that, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.444,
          "end": 290.073,
          "en": "requireUserSession needs the request object as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 293.43,
          "en": "So we have to pass that in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 293.43,
          "end": 295.44,
          "en": "We also have to do this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.44,
          "end": 297.39,
          "en": "in the loader of expenses.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 297.39,
          "end": 299.28,
          "en": "but there I am already doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 299.28,
          "end": 301.32,
          "en": "Here I forgot to do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.32,
          "end": 304.593,
          "en": "So let's save that and let's give it another try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.84,
          "end": 307.86,
          "en": "And now this looks better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 307.86,
          "end": 309.48,
          "en": "Now the expense was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 309.48,
          "end": 312.63,
          "en": "and if you take a look at it in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 312.63,
          "end": 316.08,
          "en": "you should also see that it is linked to a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 316.08,
          "end": 317.82,
          "en": "with that ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 317.82,
          "end": 321.72,
          "en": "And that ID ending with 777e",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 321.72,
          "end": 325.5,
          "en": "is indeed a valid ID of one of my users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 325.5,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "To be precise, of this user with that email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 329.763,
          "en": "with which I just logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.29,
          "end": 334.65,
          "en": "You can also tell that I'm retrieving the expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 334.65,
          "end": 338.19,
          "en": "for that user because I'm seeing my expense here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 338.19,
          "end": 340.353,
          "en": "when I look at all my expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 343.98,
          "en": "Now, for Analyze Expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 343.98,
          "end": 345.87,
          "en": "we, of course also wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 345.87,
          "end": 348.6,
          "en": "that we load the expenses of that user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 348.6,
          "end": 349.71,
          "en": "But at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 349.71,
          "end": 352.513,
          "en": "here I'm not passing my userId to getExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 353.94,
          "end": 356.43,
          "en": "It does display some data nonetheless though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 356.43,
          "end": 357.903,
          "en": "which it really shouldn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 358.8,
          "end": 362.97,
          "en": "The reason for that is that if userId is undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 362.97,
          "end": 364.56,
          "en": "in this where check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 367.26,
          "en": "Prisma will actually return all results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 370.44,
          "en": "It basically treats undefined as a wildcard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 370.44,
          "end": 374.46,
          "en": "so that it returns all results for all user IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 374.46,
          "end": 376.11,
          "en": "That can sometimes be what you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 376.11,
          "end": 378.36,
          "en": "but here it's not what I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 378.36,
          "end": 381.15,
          "en": "Hence, we can add a if check here in getExpenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 381.15,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "and check if we don't have a userId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 387.483,
          "en": "In which case, I wanna throw this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 388.5,
          "end": 391.98,
          "en": "Now, for this analysis page, we're failing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 391.98,
          "end": 393.48,
          "en": "And of course, I don't wanna fail,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 393.48,
